  "headline_finding": "On logit_rel_l2 (the continuous, least-noisy of the three metrics), the sensitivity-based policy beat EVERY naive layout at EVERY intermediate Q8-layer budget tested (4, 8, 12, 15, 20, 24) on prompts that were never used to build the ranking. On top1_preservation (a noisier, discrete metric) sensitivity tied or won at 5 of 6 budgets. On delta_nll it won at higher budgets (20, 24) but random_deterministic sometimes did better at lower budgets (4, 8, 12) -- a real, disclosed mixed result on that specific metric, not smoothed over."
